me like the haptic  motor whereas you don't feel anything on  the series three and the last difference  is that the side button actually sticks  out on the series 3 whereas it's flush  on both the se and the 7. now one thing  i do want to mention is that all three  of these apple watches were the largest  size at the time so the series 3 is a 42  millimeter the se is a 44 and the new  series 7 is a 45 so it actually gets  slightly taller than the old ones and  the final difference i want to mention  before we go to the back sides is that  the case is more rounded not more flat  it's more rounded this year so it kind  of like meets with the glass  so we'll definitely show you guys the  display differences in just a minute all  right now that we're on the backside  there are some big differences here the  series 3 has a composite back so it's  basically plastic and i don't know if  you can tell but it's got a lot of like  micro scratches on it now the se has a  new sapphire glass and ceramic back just  like the series 7 so they're more  scratch resistant and they look much  nicer now you'll also notice some  differences in the layout of the sensors  so the series 3 has the first gen  optical heart sensor then we have the  second gen and then finally the third  gen so it's basically going to be better  at sensing all your heart rate data and  everything like that and the series 7  also supports the new blood oxygen  monitoring feature and the nice thing is  that even the series 3 gets the high and  low heart rate notifications as well as  the irregular heart rhythm notifications  but the se and the series 7 come with  extra features like international  emergency calling fall detection noise  monitoring a compass an always-on  altimeter and an option of buying a new  model with cellular service and now that  we're done with the backs i've got them  all right here on my wrist it's  definitely not comfortable but i do want  to show off one more feature that's  exclusive t